\pard\b\f0\fs24 Ceres (Human)\b0\f1\fs18\par
\b\f0\par
Capacity:\b0\f1  Large orbital worker settlement; exact population not stated.\par
\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  Human staging ground for the early novel, John's home base, and the social/political pressure cooker behind the Europa push.\par
\b\f0 Related Characters:\b0\f1  John Walker, Shai Siante, Tao Vang, Tex Kovachnikov, Marcellus Athos, Lady Ava.\par
\b\f0 Season:\b0\f1  Constant orbital cycle around Earth; experienced as filtered artificial climate and shift-based station life.\par
\b\f0 Unique Features:\b0\f1  Began as a deep-space agriculture experiment, later expanded into the first major workers' settlement. Inner layers preserve older technology rather than replacing it outright.\par
\b\f0 Description:\b0\f1  Ceres stands for the Collective Earthwide Reconciliation Endeavour Settlement. It is described as a mother structure: a labyrinth of modules and docking stations forming a protected inner womb against the cold of space. What started as agricultural expansion became a conservative, layered industrial habitat whose workers now feel the strain of over-expansion, air and water quality issues, and falling morale.\par
\b\f0 Sights:\b0\f1  Interlinked docking rings, layered inner foundations, crowded worker traffic, and Earth's bright edge rising beyond the hull.\par
\b\f0 Sounds:\b0\f1  Transit pods, training chambers, station foot traffic and the constant hum of life-support.\par
\b\f0 Smell:\b0\f1  Filtered recycled air, printed food from the mess halls, and warm machinery.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  The CLEAR-guided economy helped build Ceres, but worker frustration over filters, water and working conditions shows the system is under pressure.\par
\b\f0 Built at:\b0\f1  Earth orbit.\par
